=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: laptop0
diagnosis_text:
**Affected component:** The static default route on `laptop0` (VLAN 20, 172.16.20.10/24).

**Mechanism:** `laptop0`'s routing table contains `default via 172.16.20.99 dev eth0`. The correct VLAN-20 gateway is `172.16.20.1`; `172.16.20.99` does not exist anywhere on segment 172.16.20.0/24. When `laptop0` attempts to send any packet to a destination outside its own subnet, the kernel performs ARP for `172.16.20.99`, which returns `FAILED` (no reply). The kernel then generates an ICMP "Destination Host Unreachable" locally — explaining exactly why the error originates from `172.16.20.10` itself, not from any router. Intra-VLAN traffic (e.g. to `172.16.20.1`) succeeds because those destinations are on-link and need no gateway.

**Localization:** `laptop0`, `eth0`. The gateway entry for `172.16.20.1` exists in its ARP cache with a valid MAC (`76:10:ab:fc:89:bb`), confirming that the VLAN-20 gateway interface on `mswitch1`/`router0` is fully operational. No DHCP client is running on `laptop0`, so this is a purely static host-side misconfiguration that is not shared by any peer.

**Root cause:** `laptop0` has a statically configured default gateway of `172.16.20.99` (non-existent) instead of the correct `172.16.20.1`, causing ARP resolution of the next hop to fail and all off-subnet traffic to be dropped at the source host.

**Fix:** Replace the incorrect default route on `laptop0` — `ip route del default; ip route add default via 172.16.20.1 dev eth0` — and persist the correct gateway in the startup network configuration.
=== END ===